                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af905d01-5c2d-38c9-876d-4d9e882c26bd",
                        "entry_id": "eb22d2e8-0a30-35d2-8345-fc127e4647f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not social."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "488b8b16-761e-40c3-ba21-a562997365a0",
                                "sense_id": "af905d01-5c2d-38c9-876d-4d9e882c26bd",
                                "text": "The municipal corporations of that universal kingdom are not morally at liberty at their pleasure, and on their speculations of a contingent improvement, wholly to separate and tear asunder the bands of their subordinate community, and to dissolve it into an unsocial, uncivil, unconnected chaos of elementary principles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2acc3fd3-27ac-4bec-a9bb-aac46d9dc0d5",
                                "sense_id": "af905d01-5c2d-38c9-876d-4d9e882c26bd",
                                "text": "He went to London, though he would have preferred remaining in the country; he gave a grand fête of some description or other every year, though he hated the noise and confusion; he filled his house with company, though his habits were even unsocial: in short, his whole life was one succession of sacrifices, but they were sacrifices without merit—they were the sacrifices of weakness, not of strength."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c89f7050-1c80-4c41-8117-171bfb74eb9e",
                                "sense_id": "af905d01-5c2d-38c9-876d-4d9e882c26bd",
                                "text": "The process which, if not checked, will abolish Man, goes on apace among Communists and Democrats no less than among Fascists. […] Once we killed bad men: now we liquidate unsocial elements."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42225067-da54-37dd-b5be-44e0dde1ddfd",
                        "entry_id": "eb22d2e8-0a30-35d2-8345-fc127e4647f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not seeking or showing the desire for the company of others; inhospitable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4161396b-7e70-4bd7-a3b1-f14bf9881735",
                                "sense_id": "42225067-da54-37dd-b5be-44e0dde1ddfd",
                                "text": "The cupbearer shrugged up his shoulders in displeasure. \"I thought to have lodged him in the solere chamber,\" said he; \"but since he is so unsocial to Christians, e'en let him take the next stall to Isaac the Jew's."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
